    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448-a5">

                <pb facs="0800" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg704"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 110.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Turner to Mr. Moore.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation, Liberia</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 3,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The undersigned, United States
                    minister-resident and consul-general, begs to invite your attention to a certain
                    decision or opinion of the supreme court of your republic, as rendered in a
                    certain case concluded at its last session, the title to which ‘case was, (I
                    think,) The Honorable the House of Representatives <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >versus</hi> The Republic of Liberia, and the subject-matter a question of
                    constitutionality, for the purpose of respectfully requesting that you consent
                    to furnish this legation with a copy of said decision or opinion of the supreme
                    court of your republic.</p>
                <p>The undersigned has the honor to be, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. MILTON TURNER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
